1. every value has a class
   type(1).__name__               int
   type(None).__name__            NoneType
   type(True).__name__            bool
   type(int).__name__             type
   type(type).__name__            type
2. an operator is a method call
   1 + 2                          3
   (1).__add__(2)                 3
   getattr(1, "__add__")(2)       3
3. None is an object with methods
   list(None) (no nil.to_a)       TypeError
   str(None)                      'None'
   repr(None)                     'None'
4. a literal is a receiver
   (3).times (no counterpart)     AttributeError
   "a".upper()                    'A'
   1.__class__ (compiled)         SyntaxError
   (1).__class__.__name__         'int'
5. the ancestor chain
   int.__mro__ names              ['int', 'object']
   type(None).__mro__ names       ['NoneType', 'object']
6. everything is an object, classes included
   isinstance(1, object)          True
   isinstance(None, object)       True
   isinstance(int, object)        True
   isinstance(int, type)          True
7. even the top level is an object
   __name__                       '__main__'
   type(sys.modules[__name__])    module
8. what a small integer cannot do
   x = 1; x.tag = 'mine'          AttributeError
